Except that there is no system-wide configuration file for Nethack.
At least for any version released so far, and devateam only knows what
there will be in the future versions..

> Since players cannot edit the record file on a multiuser system, this
> implies there is some space available for a system-wide configuration
> file. as well.

Nope.
The record and logfile are in the playground directory, without world-wide
write permissions.
The configuration file is in the user's own home directory, created and
edited by the user.
But one solution COULD be a system-wide configuration file
(that would probably be /etc/nethack on unix systems) that would allow some
settings that would not be read from the user-specific configurations..
I think that would work.

